 # Owner SDLC UI v1
 
+## Draft Owner Confirmation: 15 October 2026
+
+Source `36f7ce98a28a89e4471663ce51cf5c524e0ff225`, baseline `ddde019`, fixes
+the legacy-only stage checks in policy query, refresh, confirmation rendering and
+submit. All use one frontend review-context helper and the actual generated
+snake_case `draft_submode`; no backend rights, DTOs or API contracts change.
+
+Tracker `TaskState::ready()` accepts Draft `awaiting_confirmation` AND
+`clarification` only when its requirements/questions/evidence checks pass.
+`permissions.can_confirm` already includes the real server-side human owner check.
+The UI does not infer readiness from status, reason or submode alone, and does not
+compare a local Tracker user ID with the independent Central owner subject.
+Required-open-question/read-only contexts remain non-confirmable; brainstorming
+and other stages cannot confirm even with an inconsistent permission flag.
+Legacy Clarification remains supported. Tracker also projects legacy Clarification
+as Draft with absent/null submode: that path requires actual `can_confirm:true`,
+never an assumed default submode. Stale/fetching/error data cannot submit.
+
+**156 focused tests PASS** in API adapter, owner panel and the new context helper,
+including actual Draft awaiting/clarification responses, v2 policy fetch/selection,
+exact consent/CAS submit, refresh/stale behavior and negative modes/permissions.
+Full frontend typecheck, focused strict ESLint/Prettier and generated-client
+OpenAPI check PASS. No Cargo/Docker or backend qualification rerun.
+
+The separate current-stage full-page browser fixture is recorded below; old
+Clarification images remain legacy evidence, not proof of the Draft flow.
+
+### Current Draft Full-Page Fixture
+
+At the exact source above, **9/9 Playwright cases PASS**:
+Chromium/Firefox/WebKit at 375x812, 1920x1080 and 2560x1440. This fixture supplies
+the actual typed Draft `awaiting_confirmation` context, full requirements revision2,
+concrete PM assignment and declared v2 policy through intercepted reads. Each case
+asserts Draft, absence of legacy Clarification, actual v2 references and both
+unchecked consent/publication boxes. Only references are expanded; confirmation
+stays disabled and business writes, JS errors and unmocked origins are zero.
+
+The [generated relative-path manifest](assets/screens/sdlc-draft-awaiting-confirmation-v2-20261015-36f7ce9/manifest.json)
+records source/fixture hashes, `stage:Draft`, `draft_submode:awaiting_confirmation`,
+each viewport separately from actual PNG dimensions, and verified cleanup.
+All captures are full-page CSS scale, without pixel edits or resizing.
+
+| Browser | Actual PNG at viewport375 / 1920 / 2560 |
+| --- | --- |
+| Chromium | 375x6243 / 1920x4019 / 2560x4019 |
+| Firefox | 375x6228 / 1920x4024 / 2560x4024 |
+| WebKit | 375x6223 / 1920x4019 / 2560x4019 |
+
+Visually inspected [Chromium mobile](assets/screens/sdlc-draft-awaiting-confirmation-v2-20261015-36f7ce9/chromium-375x812-fullpage.png)
+and [Firefox desktop](assets/screens/sdlc-draft-awaiting-confirmation-v2-20261015-36f7ce9/firefox-1920x1080-fullpage.png):
+scoped references/consent controls have no clipping or overlap. All nine cases
+check 378 heading/reference bounds with no horizontal overflow. Prior 18 viewport,
+9 event full-page and 9 legacy Clarification reference images are preserved and
+hash-verified, not relabeled. The actual Draft clarification question/ready and
+non-ready states are covered by focused API/helper/component tests, not this
+awaiting-confirmation screenshot matrix.
+
+**Fixture-only, not production SSO, actual publication or live SDLC acceptance.**
+The source phase ran the 156 tests/typecheck; browser capture did not rerun them.
+Only transient API generation and Vite asset bundling prepared the preview; no
+full build, Cargo/Docker, dependency installation or backend/API edits. Own preview,
+junctions and scratch were removed; shared dependency lock remained unchanged.
+
